Usually we distinguish between:

GET

Used to retrieve data.

@GetMapping("/students")
public String students() {
    return "students";
}



POST

Used to submit data.

@PostMapping("/students")
public String saveStudent() {
    return "success";
}




Instead of:
@RequestMapping(value="/students", method=RequestMethod.GET)

we normally use:

@GetMapping("/students")
and
@PostMapping("/students")


because they're cleaner.
